WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:05.890
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for my Game of Thrones bonus video I wanted

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.620
to do something about Mereen and the east
just because episode 3 is a big Daenerys episode.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:17.020
So this is going to be a short history of
the city of Slavers Bay and the Ghiscari Empire.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.679
If you’re finding me for the first time.

00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:24.130
I do weekly bonus Game of Thrones videos as
well as episode reviews and Q&amp;As be sure to

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.390
subscribe to get everything.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.429
I even do a weekly giveaway for each episode.

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:32.570
My next one starts as soon as I post my review
for episode 3 tonight.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.320
So for this video I’ll say spoiler warning
for everything up to season 4 episode 2 and

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.440
the corresponding book chapters.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.350
Let’s start with some background on the
Ghiscari Empire.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.829
They were the big great civilization that
predated the Valyrian Empire.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:52.140
The pyramid we saw in the trailers is an example
of their architecture that’s survived to

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.140
current day.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.280
In a generalized way I think of them as like
the Egyptians, that were later occupied by

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.409
the Greeks and eventually the Romans.

00:00:59.409 --> 00:01:02.870
I think of the Valyrians as more like the
Roman Empire.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.420
The doom of Valyria just makes me think of
the fall of the Roman Empire.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.200
Although those two things happened for very
different reasons.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.729
Vaylria was physically obliterated by acts
of nature and the Roman Empire just got too

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:17.140
big to maintain effectively.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.689
Again in real life, very different.

00:01:19.689 --> 00:01:23.890
But the Ghiscari architecture mirrors a lot
of the pyramids and their Harpy statues remind

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.230
me a lot of Egyptian sphinxes.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:29.829
Most of the old Ghiscari cities were destroyed
in wars with the Valyrians which is one of

00:01:29.829 --> 00:01:33.510
the main reasons most of the visible signs
of their civilization are gone except for

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:38.689
the pyramids, statues and in some of the culture
of the slaves and unsullied.

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:42.951
I’m really excited for this week’s episode,
because we finally get to see the Unsullied

00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:47.010
fight based on these clips in the trailers.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:51.200
From a historical perspective the unsullied
kept a lot of the fighting traditions of the

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.380
Ghiscari alive.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.460
Most notably the lock-step way in which they
fight, like an Infantry.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.479
They also use a phalanx formation when they’re
not using siege engines and catapults.

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:05.880
So you can see George RR Martin is mixing
and matching bits of history.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.820
Because the unsullied descend from what you
could consider Egyptians and the phalanx was

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.440
a Greek fighting technique, you probably saw
them use it in the movie 300.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.160
Siege Engines originated in ancient Assyria
and catapults also came from ancient greece.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:25.170
The reason Daenerys has had so many slaves
to free is because slave trade is the main

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.202
source of income for most of the major cities
in the east.

00:02:27.202 --> 00:02:30.800
The reason that all got started was also because
of those wars with the Valyrians.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.610
When the Ghiscari were finally defeated, the
Valyrians sowed salt into all the soil so

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.540
that they couldn’t grow crops anymore.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.890
So everyone had to turn to something else
for income, thus you end up with the slaving

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:42.890
cities.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.240
Which include Astapor, Yunkai and Meereen.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.200
We saw those first two cities in season 3.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.670
Remember how Daenerys flame broiled everything.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:55.130
So that brings us to right now, outside the
gates of Mereen.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:03:00.130
The last stop on Daenerys quest to end the
slave trade in the east.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.890
The difference between this city and those
other two is that it’s much bigger.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:12.020
Mereen right now is as big as those other
two cities combined.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.460
Good thing she has all those Unsullied.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.730
She’s going to need them.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:18.370
Remember in episode 1 when they were on the
road and stopped to look at all those crucified

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.370
slaves.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:24.390
The Meereenese learned what Daenerys had done
and used a scorched earth defense against

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.390
her.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.390
Since they knew she was coming.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.940
That means they nailed up all those people
and destroyed the land surrounding the walls

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.290
so Daenerys wouldn’t have any natural defenses.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.261
Let’s save all the talk about the plot and
what’s going to happen next until my episode

00:03:35.261 --> 00:03:36.320
3 review video later tonight.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.490
I’ll post it after the episode airs.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:42.910
Mereen itself has some really cool physical
landmarks.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.860
There’s the Great Pyramid, which we’ve
seen.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:50.840
The Temple of Graces and The Fighting Pits.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.770
The Temple is a religous building that we
might get to see soon but the fighting pits

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.460
are exactly what they sound like.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.010
They’re part of a gladiator style combat
arena.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.760
Just like in the Greek Coliseum.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:09.170
I don’t know how fast the story in Meereen
is going to advance from episode to episode,

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:13.230
so I’m going to wait till episode reviews
to mention all the slaving families and the

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.500
different organizations like the Sons of the
Harpy.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.730
We’ve seen a little bit from inside the
city in the trailers, mostly night scenes,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.970
but imagine Astapor and Yunkai being a walk
in the park compared to the problems Daenerys

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.159
will face in Meereen.

00:04:26.159 --> 00:04:30.689
Not only does she have to defeat the cities
official forces, she’ll have to deal with

00:04:30.689 --> 00:04:34.819
the guerilla organizations and Urban Combat.

00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:39.689
Most of the fighting we’ve seen on the show
in Westeros and in the East has been open

00:04:39.689 --> 00:04:40.689
field combat.

00:04:40.689 --> 00:04:43.719
Like in big open spaces with lots of room
to move around with big swords and dragons.

00:04:43.719 --> 00:04:47.800
Urban combat is something that’s totally
new to most people from Westeros.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.080
Even the Unsullied aren’t really meant for
Urban combat.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.960
That’s where Daario comes in.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.460
Think of him as like the special forces leader
of Daenerys army.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.270
Even though I’m sure Grey Worm would do
just as well in any situation.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:03.259
But here’s a couple things that I’m really
excited to see that you guys should pay special

00:05:03.259 --> 00:05:04.400
attention to:

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.729
First, The fighting style of the Unsullied.

00:05:06.729 --> 00:05:08.479
We’ve really only seen them march.

00:05:08.479 --> 00:05:12.129
Daenerys isn’t using the rod of control
anymore but she’ll still give her orders

00:05:12.129 --> 00:05:16.159
to Grey Worm and he gives those orders to
the group leaders and so on all the way down

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:18.110
to the regular foot soldiers.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.199
Chain of command infantry style.

00:05:20.199 --> 00:05:22.660
This will look very cool in big wide open
scenes.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.729
Second, Daario’s fighting style.

00:05:24.729 --> 00:05:32.139
He’s a mercenary and I’m really interested
to see him in combat.

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:36.660
We got a look at his blades when he and Grey
Worm were having that contest in episode 1.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:42.110
He unlike Grey Worm is a capable negotiator
too, which is why he’s better for important

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:45.819
missions and Grey Worm is better for all out
open war.

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:47.210
Third, the architecture.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:52.460
I didn’t see a lot of the physical sets
they filmed all this on, but the CG in the

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:56.039
trailers doesn’t do the city justice.

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:59.789
Think of a larger, grander version of King’s
Landing.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:02.389
With a freaking pyramid in the middle of it.

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:06.569
That scene with Daenerys inside an underground
structure is also from the pyramid.

00:06:06.569 --> 00:06:10.430
So maybe not in this episode but pretty soon
we’ll get a really good tour of the city.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:14.360
If you’ve ever traveled to any of the older
cities in Europe you know what I’m talking

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.360
about.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.189
There’s just something about the buildings
that is so much cooler than cities in newer

00:06:19.189 --> 00:06:20.409
places like America.

00:06:20.409 --> 00:06:26.360
I think of Meereen as being like a mixture
of ancient Rome and ancient Egypt.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.520
But let me know what you’re most excited
to see in the episode.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:31.249
Remember, Daenerys story is only part of what’s
going on, Jon Snow and the Wildlings and Tyrion

00:06:31.249 --> 00:06:37.480
and the aftermath of the Purple Wedding are
all going on too.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:42.330
So I expect a lot of what happens in this
episode to continue directly into episode

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.330
4.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:46.120
It just seems like there’s too many things
happening for it all to start and end in a

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.120
single hour.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.710
Like I said, I’m posting my episode 3 review
after the episode airs.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:51.080
Probably about 9:30 PM Pacific Time tonight.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.629
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:06:52.629 --> 00:06:56.129
And feel free to leave me suggestions for
future bonus videos.

00:06:56.129 --> 00:06:59.979
Right now click here to catch up on last week’s
Purple Wedding and click here for my Q&amp;A video.

00:06:59.979 --> 00:07:02.150
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:02.650
High Fives!

